    "# Data Report\n",
    "\n",
    "This data report documents all datasets used in the project in order to ensure transparency, traceability and reproducibility. Since the project combines multiple statistical sources to visualise different dimensions of the generational conflict in Switzerland, particular attention is paid to the origin, structure, quality and transformation of the data.\n",
    "\n",
    "The report distinguishes between raw data and processed data. Raw data refers to the original files as obtained from public statistical sources. Processed data refers to cleaned, harmonised and transformed datasets that are used directly in the Streamlit application. This distinction is important because the original data sources often differ in structure, naming conventions, temporal coverage and level of aggregation.\n",
    "\n",
    "The purpose of this documentation is not only to describe the data technically, but also to make methodological decisions explicit. This includes the harmonisation of age groups, the selection of relevant indicators, the treatment of missing values and the limitations resulting from aggregated public data.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Raw Data\n",
    "\n",
    "The raw datasets are documented according to the three main dimensions of the project: **Who decides?**, **Who pays?**, and **Who owns?**. This thematic structure follows the logic of the final visualisation and makes it transparent which data sources are used for each analytical perspective.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Overview Raw Datasets\n",
    "\n",
    ": Overview of raw datasets used in the project. {#tbl-raw-overview}\n",
    "\n",
    "| Analytical dimension | Dataset name | Source | Storage location |\n",
    "|---|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Who pays? | Mandatory health insurance statistics (OKP/KVSTAT) | Swiss health insurance statistics, annual Excel files and ZIP archives | `data/whopays/raw_whopays/` |\n",
    "| Who pays? | AHV income data | Project-specific AHV income data file | `data/whopays/raw_whopays/ahv_einnahmen_zhaw.xlsx` |\n",
    "| Who pays? | AHV expenditure data | Swiss official statistics export | `data/whopays/raw_whopays/px-x-1305000000_103_20260416-235225.xlsx` |\n",
    "| Who pays? | Population by age and year | Swiss official population statistics export | `data/raw/px-x-0102020000_103_20260424-164251.xlsx` |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Details Raw Dataset: Who Decides\n",
    "\n",
    "This dataset is used to represent the first analytical dimension of the project: **Who decides?**. It contains information related to political participation, demographic influence or voting behaviour across different age groups. The dataset helps to analyse whether different generations participate equally in democratic decision-making processes.\n",
    "\n",
